---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="LightPhotos — a local-first, Lightroom-style photo manager"
  desc="LightPhotos is a fast, private photo manager for large libraries. Cull, rate, organize and develop your RAW files — in your browser or as a native desktop app. Nothing leaves your machine."
>
  <main class="lp-page">
    <section class="lp-hero">
      <div class="lp-glow"></div>
      <h1 class="lp-wordmark">Light<span class="lp-light">Photos</span></h1>
      <p class="lp-lede">
        A Lightroom-style photo manager that keeps everything on your own
        computer. Cull a shoot, rate and organize a big library, and develop
        your RAW files non-destructively &mdash; with no import step, no cloud
        and no account.
      </p>

      <div class="lp-cta-row">
        <a class="lp-btn" href="/app.html">Open the web app</a>
        <a class="lp-btn-ghost" href="/downloads.html">Download for desktop</a>
      </div>
      <p class="lp-cta-note">Free and open. Your photos are read straight from disk and never uploaded.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="lp-features" aria-label="What LightPhotos does">
      <div class="lp-feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="6" y="6" width="12" height="12" rx="2"/>
          <path d="M9 3v3M15 3v3M9 18v3M15 18v3M3 9h3M3 15h3M18 9h3M18 15h3"/>
        </svg>
        <h3>GPU-accelerated engine</h3>
        <p>Previews and adjustments render on the GPU, so panning, zooming and slider changes stay smooth even on large files.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <line x1="4" y1="8" x2="20" y2="8"/>
          <line x1="4" y1="16" x2="20" y2="16"/>
          <circle cx="9" cy="8" r="2.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
          <circle cx="15" cy="16" r="2.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
        </svg>
        <h3>Professional adjustments</h3>
        <p>Exposure, contrast, white balance, HSL, tone curves, sharpening and crop &mdash; the controls you expect from a serious editor.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7"/>
          <path d="M3 4v4h4"/>
        </svg>
        <h3>Non-destructive workflow</h3>
        <p>Every edit is an instruction, not a pixel change. Your originals are never touched, and any adjustment resets cleanly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="3" y="7" width="14" height="13" rx="2"/>
          <path d="M8 7V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2"/>
        </svg>
        <h3>Complete image library</h3>
        <p>Browse straight from folders on your disk. Ratings, flags, filters and metadata &mdash; with no import step to sit through.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M12 3.5l8.5 4.7-8.5 4.7L3.5 8.2z"/>
          <path d="M3.5 12.6l8.5 4.7 8.5-4.7"/>
        </svg>
        <h3>Batch operations</h3>
        <p>Copy settings, sync edits and apply presets across an entire selection in one move.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-feature">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="3" y="4.5" width="18" height="15" rx="2"/>
          <circle cx="8.5" cy="10" r="1.8"/>
          <path d="M4 17l4.5-4.5 3.5 3.5 3-3 5 5"/>
        </svg>
        <h3>Opens your RAW files</h3>
        <p>Sony ARW, Canon CR2 / CR3 and Adobe DNG, plus JPEG, HEIC and TIFF.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="run-modes">
      <div class="lp-section-head">
        <h2 id="run-modes">Two ways to run it</h2>
        <p>
          Same editor, same files on disk. Pick the browser for zero setup, or
          the desktop app for full native speed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-split">
        <article class="lp-split-card">
          <div class="lp-split-head">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/>
              <path d="M3 12h18M12 3c3 3.6 3 14.4 0 18M12 3c-3 3.6-3 14.4 0 18"/>
            </svg>
            <h3>Web</h3>
            <span class="lp-split-tag">No install</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lp-split-lede">
            Runs entirely in your browser through WebAssembly. Point it at a
            folder on your disk and start working &mdash; nothing to download,
            nothing to sign into.
          </p>
          <ul class="lp-check">
            <li>Always the current version &mdash; no installs or updates</li>
            <li>Photos are read locally and never leave your machine</li>
            <li>Works in any modern desktop browser</li>
            <li class="lp-con">Decoding and preview rendering run a little slower than native</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="lp-split-cta" href="/app.html">Open the web app <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </article>

        <article class="lp-split-card lp-split-card--accent">
          <div class="lp-split-head">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="3" y="4.5" width="18" height="12" rx="2"/>
              <path d="M8.5 20h7M12 16.5v3.5"/>
            </svg>
            <h3>Desktop</h3>
            <span class="lp-split-tag">Fastest</span>
          </div>
          <p class="lp-split-lede">
            A native application for your machine. Same interface, same files on
            disk &mdash; with a decode pipeline tuned to each platform.
          </p>
          <ul class="lp-check">
            <li>macOS uses the system ImageIO framework &mdash; significantly faster RAW decode and previews</li>
            <li>Snappier scrolling and zooming across large libraries</li>
            <li>Runs fully offline, no browser needed</li>
            <li class="lp-con">Requires a local install &mdash; macOS now, Windows and Linux coming soon</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="lp-split-cta" href="/downloads.html">See downloads <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lp-actions" aria-label="Keep exploring">
      <a class="lp-card" href="/blogs.html">
        <i class="ph-bold ph-pencil-simple" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h2>Blogs <span class="lp-go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></h2>
        <p>Write-ups on the hard parts: WebAssembly, threading, RAW decoding and color pipelines.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="lp-card" href="/docs.html">
        <i class="ph-bold ph-book-open" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h2>Help <span class="lp-go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></h2>
        <p>User guides, supported formats, keyboard shortcuts and common questions.</p>
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
